  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 330 AM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nHeading into Friday night and Saturday morning, upper level ridging \ntakes hold across the Southern Plains. Winds begin to decrease and \nskies begin to partially clear. Lows settle into the 30s and 40s \nareawide. A few of the coldest spots in the mountains may reach near \nfreezing, briefly Saturday morning before warming back up into the \n50s and 60s. Sunday morning will be about as chilly Saturday morning \nand that will begin a gradual warmup into the early part of next \nweek. Highs move into the 70s with morning lows in the 50s for \nMonday and Tuesday. Low (10-20%) rain chances move into the area \nfrom the west during that time, but beyond Friday, much of the long \nterm forecast is mainly dry. \n\n-Stickney",
